= 1. What this report is

Question (user, 2026-11-02): across the isogeny classes of ECC2K-130 and ECCp-131, do index-calculus relation yield, solve cost, resolving degree and related parameters differ between curves of one class? The study measures this with one instrument per part, the same on every curve, with an A\/A noise floor, an isomorphic-model control, a negative-control population and, where the design has one, a planted positive control (DESIGN.md; PROTOCOL.md of each part).

- *Characterization study, not an improvement.* The preregistered expectation is a null. A null closes a lead. Nothing here is an improvement over the current index-calculus baseline, and the CLAUDE.md success criterion (every verified, measured improvement over that baseline) is not engaged: no baseline cost is changed, no phase is sped up.
- *No leaderboard row and no benchmarks row.* There is no cross-method claim and no matched rho reference, so the validation gate (replay certificate, validator report, matched rho with the 5a band) does not apply. #raw("docs/ic-leaderboard.html"), #raw("docs/ic/LEADERBOARD.md"), #raw("docs/ic/leaderboard.json") and #raw("benchmarks/README.md") are not touched. Per-row gaps to rho are not computed here, by design.
- *L0 isolation.* All three parts ran locally on a loaded host (P1 about 2 workers, P2 one ecbench cell at a time, P3 at most 2 workers, other agent sessions on the same 3 to 4 cores). Counted metrics (degrees, ranks, relation counts, field multiplications, row operations, solution counts) are exact and are the only ones that decide. Clocks (#raw("cpu_s"), #raw("wall_s"), #raw("online_wall_ns_per_attempt"), #raw("dreg_s"), #raw("build_s")) are descriptive only and decide nothing.
- *Deferred, not dropped.* P1 tier 2 (#raw("m2t4")), P2 at 36 and 40 bits (8 cells) and P3a-Y (n=43, k=13 yield line, claim C3) were not run under the amended protocols. They stay in the preregistration and are reported as "not run (deferred)", never filled.
- *Pending cells.* Cells still running at generation time show as "pending" in tables and graphs, never as nulls or zeros. Rerun #raw("report/build.sh") when the runs finish.


