== 5.1 What it shows now

- *Measured.* In every cell, every arm other than AA\_perm has ratio to E0 within 3.850e-5 of 1 on D\_solve, first fall degree, final rank and field mults (the largest deviation over all cells and these four metrics is 3.850e-5; 0 means the recorded ratio is exactly 1). The arms present are the Elkies neighbours, the isomorphic model and the random non-isogenous curves (27 each, minus the planted instances that were not formed), for configs m2t3 and m3t2 and kinds null, planted and ladder.
- *Measured.* The arm that moves the operation count is AA\_perm (field\_mults ratio 0.976 to 1.165 over the cells in which it appears); its D\_solve and final rank ratios deviate from 1 by at most 0. By construction (PROTOCOL section 3) this arm is the E0 instance with a seeded permutation of the variable order, the re-encoding noise floor: it sets how far the operation count moves under a re-encoding of the same curve, and it is not a curve effect.
- *Measured, descriptive.* #raw("cpu_s") ratios of arms other than AA\_perm lie within 0.074 of 1 (cells above); AA\_perm cpu ratio 0.985 to 1.121. The clock was taken at L0 on a loaded host and decides nothing.
- *Measured.* 1008 planted rows were not formed (see table); they are missing, not zero.

*Reading (main session, 2026-11-02; interpretation, labelled as such).* At 131 bits the instrument's counted profile (XL closure degree, rank, field multiplications, per-degree profiles) is independent of the curve: it is the same on the 27 neighbours, on the isomorphic model and on the 27 random non-isogenous curves. Because random non-isogenous curves match as well, the null population is uninformative about isogeny specifically: this instrument at this system size does not distinguish any curve from any other, so it cannot see an isogeny-class effect even if one existed in a quantity it does not count. #raw("D_solve") is the XL\/Macaulay closure degree of this study's engine; on the 147 comparable mirror systems of #raw("p1_eccp131/CROSSCHECK.md") it is strictly above F4's top step degree, so it is not F4's solving degree and not a degree of regularity, and no statement here calls it one. Full-width yield is predicted, not observed (exact-curve screens found zero relations).


