= 9. Reproduce, inputs and files

Rerun from the repository root: #raw("research/isogeny_class_ic_yield_20261102/report/build.sh"). It compiles #raw("report/gen/gen_report.rs") (Rust, std only, #raw("rustc -O")), pools the P3 shards and archives the masked then unmasked #raw("p3h analyze") outputs under #raw("report/data/p3_analysis/") (needs the built #raw("target/release/p3h"); skipped with a note if absent), runs the generator and renders #raw("REPORT.pdf") from #raw("REPORT.typ") with Typst. Typst is document rendering only; if it is not installed the script installs the #raw("typst") wheel in a scratch virtualenv outside the repository, as the research-visuals skill prescribes. No Python computes any value in this report.

- #raw("report/REPORT.md"), #raw("report/REPORT.typ"), #raw("report/REPORT.pdf"): this report in three forms (generated, do not edit by hand).
- #raw("report/figures/*.svg") with #raw("*.data.tsv") beside each: class\_structure, p1\_arm\_ratio\_strip, p2\_yield\_per\_curve, p3\_dreg\_n131, p3\_dreg\_n43.
- #raw("report/data/inputs.sha256.tsv"): sha256 of every input file read in this build.
- #raw("report/data/p3_analysis/"): #raw("p3h analyze") text output per pooled P3 file family (masked first, then unmasked).

